{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"The curator (harvest H5): re-verifies STALE claims against their referents' CURRENT content - store facets or registered-repo files ({repo,path} via the dev.git registry). confirm re-stamps the source hash (and, on repo sources, the HEAD commit; stale clears), marks reverified, steps confidence up - drift checked and survived is evidence; amend decays the old and remembers the corrected text with a fresh same-shape stamp; retire decays toward the review queue. One-memory-cycle A1/A2: claims are located in the facet+overlay union; on a SHIPPED domain the confirm re-stamp is a superseding overlay line (committed bytes untouched), local domains keep the journaled in-place write; traces go to the local traces log unconditionally. One frontier call per claim, limit-capped.","import":"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse ndata::data::Data;\nuse flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::time::time;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::system_call::system_call;\nuse crate::agent::archivist::epistemic_work::epistemic_work;\nuse crate::agent::archivist::decay::decay;\nuse crate::agent::archivist::remember::remember;\nuse crate::agent::llm::ask_llm::ask_llm;","params":[{"desc":"How many stale claims to re-verify this run (1-10; one frontier call each). The act-sized default is 1 - the drive tick's portion.","name":"limit","type":"Integer"}],"returntype":"JSONObject","type":"rust"},"id":"xknmpg1a01a30b0bdw1","readers":[],"time":1787320391972,"username":"system","writers":[]}